module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.Pretopology
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Syntomic.BaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ExtendingFunctorsLimits
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.StandardRefinement

/-!
# Extending functors from a full subcategory of schemes: the five standard topologies

Let `S` be a scheme, let `𝒞` be a full subcategory of `Sch/S` satisfying conditions (1) and (2)
of Stacks 0EUW and let `F : 𝒞ᵒᵖ ⥤ Set` satisfy conditions (a) and (b). The extension
`F' = AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.extension` of `F` to `Sch/S`, constructed in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ExtendingFunctorsExistence` and shown to be a Zariski
sheaf in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ExtendingFunctorsSheaf`, is a sheaf for each
of the five topologies — Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic and fppf — as soon as `F` satisfies
the sheaf condition for the standard coverings of that topology on the affines of finite
presentation over an affine open of `S`.

This file formalizes the general case of the source's proof: the passage from the standard
coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine open of `S` to all coverings of all objects.
The five topologies are treated uniformly by quantifying over
`AlgebraicGeometry.CoveringTopology`.

## The reduction

An object `X` of `Sch/S` is covered by its affine opens lying over affine opens of `S`. Over such
an affine open `U` a given `τ`-covering of `X` pulls back to a `τ`-covering of `U`, which Stacks
03XA refines by a *standard* `τ`-covering; the restricted sheaf condition then produces a section
over `U`, and that section is characterized by agreeing with the given family on every morphism
into `U` factoring through a member of the covering over `X`. This characterization is what makes
the local sections agree on the pairwise intersections and makes the glued section restrict
correctly to the members of the covering; both are the verifications the source omits. The
gluing itself is the Zariski sheaf condition.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.coveringPrecoverage`: the precoverage of `τ`-coverings on
  `Sch/S`, obtained from Mathlib's precoverage of jointly surjective families with the morphism
  property of the topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.IsCoveringSheaf`: the conclusion of the source, the sheaf
  condition for every `τ`-covering of every object of `Sch/S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.IsStandardAffineSheaf`: the restricted sheaf condition, for
  the standard `τ`-coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.IsStandardAffineSheafOnSubcategory`: condition (c) of the
  source, for a functor on the full subcategory.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage`: a `τ`-covering
  of `Sch/S` base changes to a `τ`-covering.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_of_isStandardCovering`: a
  standard `τ`-covering of an affine object is a `τ`-covering.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.exists_standardCovering_refinement_over`: Stacks 03XA for
  `Sch/S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isSeparatedFor_of_isStandardAffineSheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.exists_section_of_isStandardAffineSheaf`: the two halves of
  the reduction.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isCoveringSheaf_of_isStandardAffineSheaf`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isCoveringSheaf_extension`: the reduction and its instance
  at the extension.

## Implementation notes

A `τ`-covering is a family of morphisms rather than a covering sieve, matching the source, and
its index type is in an arbitrary universe. Since `Sch/S` has pullbacks,
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by such a family is the condition
that the value at the target be the equalizer of the two maps between the products over the
members and over their pairwise fibre products.

The sheaf condition for the standard `τ`-coverings of the affine objects of `Sch/S` lying over an
affine open of `S` is carried as a hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isCoveringSheaf_extension` rather than deduced from
condition (c): the source's deduction writes such an affine object as a directed limit of affines
of finite presentation over an affine open of `S` (Stacks 00QN,
`AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.exists_lfpPresentation`), descends the standard covering to a
stage of that limit (Stacks 049N) and passes to the filtered colimit, and that argument is not
formalized here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GDW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GDW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EUW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EUW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03XA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03XA)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors

universe w u v

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Coverings for the five standard topologies on `Sch/S` -/

theorem isStableUnderBaseChange_coveringMorphismProperty (τ : CoveringTopology) :
    (coveringMorphismProperty.{u} τ).IsStableUnderBaseChange := by
  cases τ with
  | fppf => exact MorphismProperty.IsStableUnderBaseChange.inf
  | syntomic => exact syntomic_isStableUnderBaseChange
  | smooth => infer_instance
  | etale => infer_instance
  | zariski => infer_instance

/-- The precoverage of `τ`-coverings on `Sch/S`. -/
def coveringPrecoverage (S : Scheme.{u}) (τ : CoveringTopology) : Precoverage (Over S) :=
  (Scheme.precoverage (coveringMorphismProperty.{u} τ)).comap (Over.forget S)

instance isStableUnderBaseChange_coveringPrecoverage (S : Scheme.{u}) (τ : CoveringTopology) :
    (coveringPrecoverage S τ).IsStableUnderBaseChange := by
  have h := isStableUnderBaseChange_coveringMorphismProperty.{u} τ
  have : (Scheme.precoverage (coveringMorphismProperty.{u} τ)).IsStableUnderBaseChange := by
    rw [Scheme.precoverage]; infer_instance
  rw [coveringPrecoverage]
  infer_instance

lemma ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_iff (τ : CoveringTopology) {X : Over S} {ι : Type v}
    (Y : ι → Over S) (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X) :
    Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ X ↔
      (∀ x : X.left, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (f i).left) ∧
        ∀ i, coveringMorphismProperty τ (f i).left := by
  rw [coveringPrecoverage, Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, Presieve.map_ofArrows,
    Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff]
  rfl

/-- Base change of a `τ`-covering of `Sch/S` along an arbitrary morphism. -/
lemma ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage (τ : CoveringTopology) {X : Over S} {ι : Type v}
    {Y : ι → Over S} (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X)
    (hf : Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ X) {Z : Over S} (g : Z ⟶ X) :
    Presieve.ofArrows (fun i => pullback g (f i)) (fun i => pullback.fst g (f i)) ∈
      coveringPrecoverage S τ Z :=
  Precoverage.mem_coverings_of_isPullback f hf g _ (fun i => pullback.snd g (f i))
    fun i => IsPullback.of_hasPullback g (f i)


/-! ### The sheaf conditions -/

/-- **The conclusion of Stacks 0GDW.** A functor on `Sch/S` satisfies the sheaf condition for
every `τ`-covering `{Y i ⟶ X}` of every object of `Sch/S`.

Since `Sch/S` has pullbacks, `CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor` for the presieve generated by
the family is the condition that `G X` be the equalizer of the two maps
`∏ G (Y i) ⟶ ∏ G (Y i ×_X Y j)`. -/
def IsCoveringSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology) (G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w) : Prop :=
  ∀ {ι : Type v} (X : Over S) (Y : ι → Over S) (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X),
    Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ X → (Presieve.ofArrows Y f).IsSheafFor G

/-- The sheaf condition for a functor on `Sch/S` and the *standard* `τ`-coverings of the affine
objects of `Sch/S` whose structure morphism factors through an affine open of `S`.

This is the restricted case of `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.IsCoveringSheaf` to which the
general case is reduced in
`AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isCoveringSheaf_of_isStandardAffineSheaf`. -/
def IsStandardAffineSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology) (G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w) : Prop :=
  ∀ {ι : Type v} (V : Over S) (hV : IsAffineOverAffineOpen V) (W : ι → Over S)
    (f : ∀ i, W i ⟶ V),
    @IsStandardCovering τ V.left hV.1 ι (fun i => (W i).left) (fun i => (f i).left) →
      (Presieve.ofArrows W f).IsSheafFor G

/-- **Condition (c) of Stacks 0GDW.** For every standard `τ`-covering `{V i ⟶ V}` of affines in
`Sch/S` whose target is an object of the full subcategory with `V ⟶ S` factoring through an
affine open `U ⊆ S` by a morphism of finite presentation, the sheaf condition holds for `F` and
`{V i ⟶ V}`.

The footnote of the source observes that this is meaningful because condition (2) makes `V`, the
`V i` and the `V i ×_V V j` isomorphic to objects of the full subcategory; accordingly the
members of the covering are taken to be objects of the full subcategory, while the pairwise
fibre products — which again lie in it up to isomorphism, so that the subcategory has the
relevant pullbacks — are left to
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.IsSheafFor`, whose compatibility condition on a family of sections is
tested on every object of the subcategory mapping to two members of the covering. -/
def IsStandardAffineSheafOnSubcategory (τ : CoveringTopology) (P : ObjectProperty (Over S))
    (F : P.FullSubcategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w) : Prop :=
  ∀ {ι : Type v} (V : P.FullSubcategory) (hV : IsAffine V.obj.left) (U : S.affineOpens)
    (g : V.obj.left ⟶ U.1.toScheme) (_ : g ≫ U.1.ι = V.obj.hom) (_ : FinitePresentation g)
    (W : ι → P.FullSubcategory) (f : ∀ i, W i ⟶ V),
    @IsStandardCovering τ V.obj.left hV ι (fun i => (W i).obj.left)
        (fun i => (P.ι.map (f i)).left) →
      (Presieve.ofArrows W f).IsSheafFor F

/-! ### Sections of a sheaf for a family of arrows -/

/-- The amalgamation of an indexed family of sections for a presieve generated by arrows.

`CategoryTheory.Presieve.FamilyOfElements` is indexed by the arrows of the presieve rather than by
the index type of the generating family, so this restates the sheaf condition in terms of the
index type. -/
theorem exists_section_of_isSheafFor_ofArrows {C : Type*} [Category C] {G : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w}
    {X : C} {ι : Type*} (W : ι → C) (g : ∀ j, W j ⟶ X)
    (hsh : (Presieve.ofArrows W g).IsSheafFor G) (y : ∀ j, G.obj (op (W j)))
    (hy : ∀ (j j' : ι) (A : C) (a : A ⟶ W j) (b : A ⟶ W j'), a ≫ g j = b ≫ g j' →
      G.map a.op (y j) = G.map b.op (y j')) :
    ∃ t : G.obj (op X), ∀ j, G.map (g j).op t = y j := by
  classical
  let x : Presieve.FamilyOfElements G (Presieve.ofArrows W g) :=
    fun A h hh => G.map (eqToHom hh.obj_idx.symm).op (y hh.idx)
  have hxval : ∀ (A : C) (h : A ⟶ X) (hh : Presieve.ofArrows W g h),
      x h hh = G.map (eqToHom hh.obj_idx.symm).op (y hh.idx) := fun _ _ _ => rfl
  have hfac : ∀ (A : C) (h : A ⟶ X) (hh : Presieve.ofArrows W g h),
      eqToHom hh.obj_idx.symm ≫ g hh.idx = h :=
    fun _ _ hh => hh.eq_eqToHom_comp_hom_idx.symm
  have hcomp : x.Compatible := by
    intro A₁ A₂ Z k₁ k₂ h₁ h₂ hh₁ hh₂ hk
    rw [hxval, hxval, map_map_apply, map_map_apply]
    refine hy _ _ Z _ _ ?_
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hfac _ _ hh₁, hfac _ _ hh₂, hk]
  obtain ⟨t, ht, -⟩ := hsh x hcomp
  refine ⟨t, fun j => ?_⟩
  have hj := ht (g j) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk j)
  rw [hxval] at hj
  rw [hj]
  have := hy (Presieve.ofArrows.mk (f := g) j).idx j (W j)
    (eqToHom (Presieve.ofArrows.mk (f := g) j).obj_idx.symm) (𝟙 (W j))
    (by rw [Category.id_comp]; exact hfac _ _ (Presieve.ofArrows.mk j))
  rw [this, map_id_apply]


/-! ### Standard coverings are coverings -/

/-- Each member of a standard `τ`-covering has the property of morphisms defining the topology. -/
lemma coveringMorphismProperty_of_isStandardCovering (τ : CoveringTopology) {T : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsAffine T] {ι : Type v} {U : ι → Scheme.{u}} {f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T}
    (h : IsStandardCovering τ U f) (i : ι) : coveringMorphismProperty τ (f i) := by
  have hUi : IsAffine (U i) := h.affine_source i
  cases τ with
  | fppf => exact ⟨(h.standard i).1, (h.standard i).2.1⟩
  | syntomic => exact syntomic_of_standardSyntomic (h.standard i)
  | smooth =>
      exact (HasRingHomProperty.iff_of_isAffine (P := @Smooth)).2
        (RingHom.IsStandardSmooth.smooth (h.standard i))
  | etale => exact h.standard i
  | zariski =>
      obtain ⟨a, e, he⟩ := h.standard i
      rw [he]
      infer_instance

/-- A standard `τ`-covering of an affine object of `Sch/S` is a `τ`-covering. -/
lemma ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_of_isStandardCovering (τ : CoveringTopology) {V : Over S}
    (hV : IsAffine V.left) {ι : Type v} (W : ι → Over S) (f : ∀ i, W i ⟶ V)
    (h : @IsStandardCovering τ V.left hV ι (fun i => (W i).left) (fun i => (f i).left)) :
    Presieve.ofArrows W f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ V := by
  rw [ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_iff]
  refine ⟨fun x => ?_, fun i => coveringMorphismProperty_of_isStandardCovering τ h i⟩
  have hx : x ∈ ⋃ i, Set.range (f i).left := by
    rw [h.jointly_surjective]; trivial
  exact Set.mem_iUnion.mp hx

/-- **Stacks 03XA for `Sch/S`.** A `τ`-covering of an affine object of `Sch/S` is refined by a
standard `τ`-covering, the refinement being recorded as a choice of index and of a morphism over
the target for each member. -/
lemma exists_standardCovering_refinement_over (τ : CoveringTopology) {V : Over S}
    (hV : IsAffine V.left) {ι : Type v} {Y : ι → Over S} (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ V)
    (hf : Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ V) :
    ∃ (κ : Type v) (W : κ → Over S) (g : ∀ j, W j ⟶ V) (a : κ → ι) (c : ∀ j, W j ⟶ Y (a j)),
      (@IsStandardCovering τ V.left hV κ (fun j => (W j).left) (fun j => (g j).left)) ∧
        ∀ j, g j = c j ≫ f (a j) := by
  have := hV
  let E : PreZeroHypercover.{v} V.left :=
    { I₀ := ι, X := fun i => (Y i).left, f := fun i => (f i).left }
  have hE : E.presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.precoverage (coveringMorphismProperty τ) V.left := by
    obtain ⟨hsurj, hprop⟩ := (ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_iff τ Y f).mp hf
    exact (Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff _).mpr ⟨hsurj, hprop⟩
  obtain ⟨Wh, r, hstd⟩ := exists_standardCovering_refinement τ E hE
  refine ⟨Wh.I₀, fun j => Over.mk (Wh.f j ≫ V.hom), fun j => Over.homMk (Wh.f j) rfl,
    fun j => r.s₀ j, fun j => Over.homMk (r.h₀ j) ?_, hstd, fun j => ?_⟩
  · show r.h₀ j ≫ (Y (r.s₀ j)).hom = Wh.f j ≫ V.hom
    rw [← Over.w (f (r.s₀ j)), ← Category.assoc]
    exact congrArg (· ≫ V.hom) (r.w₀ j)
  · refine Over.OverMorphism.ext ?_
    rw [Over.comp_left]
    exact (r.w₀ j).symm


/-! ### The reduction to the standard affine case -/

/-- A map factoring through the base change of `f` along `p` becomes, after composing with `p`,
a map factoring through `f`. -/
private theorem comp_eq_of_eq_comp_pullback_fst {X Y U W : Over S} (p : U ⟶ X) (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (g : W ⟶ U) (c : W ⟶ pullback p f) (h : g = c ≫ pullback.fst p f) :
    g ≫ p = (c ≫ pullback.snd p f) ≫ f := by
  rw [h, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, pullback.condition]

/-- **Separatedness for all `τ`-coverings.** A Zariski sheaf on `Sch/S` which satisfies the sheaf
condition for the standard `τ`-coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine open of `S`
is separated for every `τ`-covering.

This is the uniqueness half of the general case of the proof of Stacks 0GDW: a section is
determined by its restrictions to an affine open covering of its domain lying over affine opens
of `S`, and over each such affine open the given covering is refined by a standard one. -/
theorem isSeparatedFor_of_isStandardAffineSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology)
    {G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w} (haG : IsZariskiSheaf G)
    (hG : IsStandardAffineSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G) {ι : Type v} (X : Over S) (Y : ι → Over S)
    (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X) (hf : Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ X) :
    (Presieve.ofArrows Y f).IsSeparatedFor G := by
  intro x u₁ u₂ hu₁ hu₂
  have hagree : ∀ i, G.map (f i).op u₁ = G.map (f i).op u₂ := fun i => by
    rw [hu₁ (f i) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i), hu₂ (f i) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i)]
  obtain ⟨κ₀, V, hVcov, hVaff⟩ := exists_isAffineOverAffineOpen_cover X
  refine zariskiSheaf_ext haG V hVcov u₁ u₂ fun k => ?_
  obtain ⟨κ, W, g, a, c, hstd, hgc⟩ := exists_standardCovering_refinement_over τ (hVaff k).1
    (fun i => pullback.fst (overOpenι X (V k)) (f i))
    (ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage τ f hf (overOpenι X (V k)))
  refine (hG _ (hVaff k) W g hstd).isSeparatedFor.ext ?_
  intro A h hh
  obtain ⟨j⟩ := hh
  rw [map_map_apply, map_map_apply, comp_eq_of_eq_comp_pullback_fst _ _ _ _ (hgc j),
    ← map_map_apply, hagree, map_map_apply]


/-- **The section over an affine object.** Let `{Y i ⟶ X}` be a `τ`-covering and let `s` be a
family of sections of `G` over the `Y i` agreeing on every object of `Sch/S` mapping to two
members of the covering. For an affine object `U` of `Sch/S` lying over an affine open of `S`
together with a morphism `U ⟶ X`, there is a section of `G` over `U` which agrees with the given
family on every morphism into `U` that factors through a member of the covering over `X`.

This is the affine case of the general step of the proof of Stacks 0GDW: the covering is pulled
back to `U` and refined there by a standard `τ`-covering, over whose members the family supplies
compatible sections. The characterizing property also discharges the two compatibility
verifications omitted by the source. -/
theorem exists_section_of_isStandardAffineSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology)
    {G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w} (haG : IsZariskiSheaf G)
    (hG : IsStandardAffineSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G) {ι : Type v} {X : Over S} {Y : ι → Over S}
    (f : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X) (hf : Presieve.ofArrows Y f ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ X)
    (s : ∀ i, G.obj (op (Y i)))
    (hs : ∀ (i i' : ι) (A : Over S) (α : A ⟶ Y i) (β : A ⟶ Y i'),
      α ≫ f i = β ≫ f i' → G.map α.op (s i) = G.map β.op (s i'))
    {U : Over S} (hU : IsAffineOverAffineOpen U) (p : U ⟶ X) :
    ∃ t : G.obj (op U), ∀ (Z : Over S) (q : Z ⟶ U) (i : ι) (r : Z ⟶ Y i),
      q ≫ p = r ≫ f i → G.map q.op t = G.map r.op (s i) := by
  obtain ⟨κ, W, g, a, c, hstd, hgc⟩ := exists_standardCovering_refinement_over τ hU.1
    (fun i => pullback.fst p (f i)) (ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage τ f hf p)
  -- the refinement maps to the members of the covering over `X`
  have hgd := fun j => comp_eq_of_eq_comp_pullback_fst p (f (a j)) (g j) (c j) (hgc j)
  -- the sections of `G` over the members of the refinement, and their coherence
  have hy : ∀ (j j' : κ) (A : Over S) (α : A ⟶ W j) (β : A ⟶ W j'), α ≫ g j = β ≫ g j' →
      G.map α.op (G.map (c j ≫ pullback.snd p (f (a j))).op (s (a j)))
        = G.map β.op (G.map (c j' ≫ pullback.snd p (f (a j'))).op (s (a j'))) := by
    intro j j' A α β hαβ
    rw [map_map_apply, map_map_apply]
    refine hs _ _ A _ _ ?_
    simp only [Category.assoc] at hgd ⊢
    rw [← hgd j, ← hgd j', ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, hαβ]
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := exists_section_of_isSheafFor_ofArrows W g (hG _ hU W g hstd)
    (fun j => G.map (c j ≫ pullback.snd p (f (a j))).op (s (a j))) hy
  refine ⟨t, fun Z q i r hqr => ?_⟩
  -- the standard refinement is itself a `τ`-covering, so its base change to `Z` separates `G`
  have hWcov : Presieve.ofArrows W g ∈ coveringPrecoverage S τ U :=
    ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_of_isStandardCovering τ hU.1 W g hstd
  refine (isSeparatedFor_of_isStandardAffineSheaf τ haG hG Z _
    (fun j => pullback.fst q (g j))
    (ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage τ g hWcov q)).ext ?_
  intro A h hh
  obtain ⟨j⟩ := hh
  have h₁ : pullback.fst q (g j) ≫ q = pullback.snd q (g j) ≫ g j := pullback.condition
  have h₂ : (pullback.snd q (g j) ≫ (c j ≫ pullback.snd p (f (a j)))) ≫ f (a j)
      = (pullback.fst q (g j) ≫ r) ≫ f i := by
    simp only [Category.assoc] at hgd ⊢
    rw [← hgd j, ← hqr, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, ← h₁]
  rw [map_map_apply, map_map_apply, h₁, ← map_map_apply, ht j, map_map_apply]
  exact hs _ _ _ _ _ h₂


/-- **The reduction of Stacks 0GDW to the standard affine case.** A Zariski sheaf on `Sch/S`
which satisfies the sheaf condition for the standard `τ`-coverings of the affine objects lying
over an affine open of `S` satisfies the sheaf condition for every `τ`-covering.

This is the general case of the proof of the source. An object of `Sch/S` is covered by its
affine opens lying over affine opens of `S`; over each of them the given covering is refined by a
standard `τ`-covering, which produces a local section
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.exists_section_of_isStandardAffineSheaf`); the local
sections agree on the pairwise intersections because both restrictions are computed by the given
family over the base change of the covering to the intersection, and they glue by the Zariski
sheaf condition. -/
@[stacks 0GDW "the general case of the source's proof: a Zariski sheaf on Sch/S which is a sheaf
for the standard τ-coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine open of the base is a
sheaf for every τ-covering"]
theorem isCoveringSheaf_of_isStandardAffineSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology)
    {G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w} (haG : IsZariskiSheaf G)
    (hG : IsStandardAffineSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G) : IsCoveringSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G := by
  intro ι X Yc f hf
  refine (isSeparatedFor_of_isStandardAffineSheaf τ haG hG X Yc f hf).isSheafFor ?_
  intro x hx
  have hs : ∀ (i i' : ι) (A : Over S) (α : A ⟶ Yc i) (β : A ⟶ Yc i'), α ≫ f i = β ≫ f i' →
      G.map α.op (x (f i) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i))
        = G.map β.op (x (f i') (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i')) :=
    fun i i' A α β h => hx α β (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i') h
  obtain ⟨κ₀, V, hVcov, hVaff⟩ := exists_isAffineOverAffineOpen_cover X
  choose tt htt using fun k : κ₀ => exists_section_of_isStandardAffineSheaf τ haG hG f hf
    (fun i => x (f i) (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i)) hs (hVaff k) (overOpenι X (V k))
  -- the local sections agree on the pairwise intersections
  have hcompat : ∀ k l : κ₀,
      G.map (overOpenLE X (inf_le_left : V k ⊓ V l ≤ V k)).op (tt k)
        = G.map (overOpenLE X (inf_le_right : V k ⊓ V l ≤ V l)).op (tt l) := by
    intro k l
    refine (isSeparatedFor_of_isStandardAffineSheaf τ haG hG (overOpen X (V k ⊓ V l)) _
      (fun i => pullback.fst (overOpenι X (V k ⊓ V l)) (f i))
      (ofArrows_pullback_mem_coveringPrecoverage τ f hf (overOpenι X (V k ⊓ V l)))).ext ?_
    intro A h hh
    obtain ⟨i⟩ := hh
    have e₁ : ∀ {W : X.left.Opens} (hW : V k ⊓ V l ≤ W),
        (pullback.fst (overOpenι X (V k ⊓ V l)) (f i) ≫ overOpenLE X hW) ≫ overOpenι X W
          = pullback.snd (overOpenι X (V k ⊓ V l)) (f i) ≫ f i := fun hW => by
      rw [Category.assoc, overOpenLE_comp_overOpenι, pullback.condition]
    rw [map_map_apply, map_map_apply, htt k _ _ i _ (e₁ inf_le_left),
      htt l _ _ i _ (e₁ inf_le_right)]
  obtain ⟨t, hts, -⟩ := haG X κ₀ V hVcov tt hcompat
  refine ⟨t, ?_⟩
  intro A h hh
  obtain ⟨i⟩ := hh
  -- the glued section restricts to the given family over each member of the covering
  refine zariskiSheaf_ext haG (fun k : κ₀ => (f i).left ⁻¹ᵁ V k) ?_ _ _ fun k => ?_
  · rw [← Scheme.Hom.preimage_iSup, hVcov, Scheme.Hom.preimage_top]
  have hr : Set.range (⇑(overOpenι (Yc i) ((f i).left ⁻¹ᵁ V k) ≫ f i).left)
      ⊆ ((V k : X.left.Opens) : Set X.left) := by
    rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
    exact y.2
  have hlift := liftOverOpen_comp_overOpenι (overOpenι (Yc i) ((f i).left ⁻¹ᵁ V k) ≫ f i) (V k) hr
  rw [map_map_apply, ← hlift, ← map_map_apply, hts k,
    htt k _ _ i (overOpenι (Yc i) ((f i).left ⁻¹ᵁ V k)) hlift]


/-- The sheaf condition for the standard `τ`-coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine
open of `S` is weaker than the sheaf condition for all `τ`-coverings: the coverings it tests are
`τ`-coverings of a restricted class of objects.

Together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.isCoveringSheaf_of_isStandardAffineSheaf` this identifies
the two conditions for a Zariski sheaf. -/
theorem isStandardAffineSheaf_of_isCoveringSheaf (τ : CoveringTopology)
    {G : (Over S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w} (h : IsCoveringSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G) :
    IsStandardAffineSheaf.{w, u, v} τ G := fun V hV W f hstd =>
  h V W f (ofArrows_mem_coveringPrecoverage_of_isStandardCovering τ hV.1 W f hstd)

/-! ### The extension of a functor from a full subcategory -/

/-- **Stacks 0GDW, the general case of the source's proof, at the extension.** Let `S` be a
scheme, let `𝒞` be a full subcategory of `Sch/S` satisfying conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks
0EUW and let `F : 𝒞ᵒᵖ ⥤ Set` satisfy condition (a). Then the extension
`F' = AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors.extension` of `F` to `Sch/S` satisfies the sheaf
condition for every `τ`-covering as soon as it satisfies the sheaf condition for the standard
`τ`-coverings of the affine objects of `Sch/S` lying over an affine open of `S`.

The source deduces the latter from its condition (c) by writing such an affine object as a
directed limit of affines of finite presentation over an affine open of `S` (Stacks 00QN),
descending the standard covering to a stage of that limit (Stacks 049N) and passing to the
filtered colimit; that deduction is not formalized here, so the restricted sheaf condition is
carried as the hypothesis `hstd`. -/
@[stacks 0GDW "the general case: the extension is a sheaf for every τ-covering once it is one for
the standard τ-coverings of the affine objects lying over an affine open of the base, which is
carried as a hypothesis"]
theorem isCoveringSheaf_extension (τ : CoveringTopology) (P : ObjectProperty (Over S))
    (F : P.FullSubcategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (max w (u + 1))) (hP1 : HasAffineOpens P)
    (hP2 : HasFinitePresentationAffines P) (haF : IsZariskiSheafOnSubcategory P F)
    (hstd : IsStandardAffineSheaf.{max w (u + 1), u, v} τ (extension P F)) :
    IsCoveringSheaf.{max w (u + 1), u, v} τ (extension P F) :=
  isCoveringSheaf_of_isStandardAffineSheaf τ (isZariskiSheaf_extension P F hP1 hP2 haF) hstd

end AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendingFunctors

